    "reviewed_contracts": [
      "Eligible first must select itself; fixed BatchIndices bound rejects invalid limit, candidate count or oversized completion before marking any prefix. Zero completion throws; no retry loop.",
      "Selection maintains existing original candidate order and exact compatibility. Natural admission may shrink only a selected prefix; teacher-forced zero-row cache hits stay ineligible.",
      "Both consumers retain original execution/observer/ledger logic. Generic callbacks neither admit/retire requests nor own payloads, model state, RNG, Completion or rollback.",
      "Same-wave checkpoint lookup preparation precedes all dispatch and publication remains after all dispatch; new heads cannot feed a peer in the same wave.",
      "Observer/accounting exceptions exit immediately. The new helper marks local dispatch completion after adapter bookkeeping; unlike old mark position, an exception can leave indices unmarked after actual commit, but there is no resumed pass/retry and model ledger reconciliation remains authoritative.",
      "RequestWindow active borrow is not mutated in dispatch; release/retirement follows after the wave. Borrowed selected indices are used synchronously and not retained.",
      "Core uses static callables and original cold index storage; it introduces no vector, virtual/type-erased call, queue, worker or executor."
    ],
